Task: Harden movie matching for release-style filenames (c1a7f4d2)

Summary:
- Fixed ImportManager movie matching for completed torrents whose filenames contain release metadata (e.g. The.Matrix.1999.1080p.BrRip.x264.YIFY.mp4).
- Replaced reversed/overly-broad title matching with parsed title/year matching and normalized clean-title fallback.
- Added a regression test that validates year-prioritized matching for dot-delimited release names.
- Recorded the completed hardening task in the active Conductor plan for import_pipeline_20260228.

Files changed:
- server/src/services/ImportManager.ts
- server/src/services/ImportManager.test.ts
- conductor/tracks/import_pipeline_20260228/plan.md

Why:
- Import failures were logged as "No match found" for known library movies because the query attempted to match full release strings against stored movie titles.
- The new parsing/matching logic aligns import matching behavior with release-name reality while preserving existing import flows.

